.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Vt dtfl_collection
is a timely dataflow stream whose records are differential updates: a
.Pq record , time , diff
triple that says how the multiplicity of
.Va record
changes by
.Va diff
at logical time
.Va time .
The collection operators build new collections from old ones, each
transforming the record, time or diff part of every update.
.Pp
A
.Vt dtfl_diff
is the algebra of a collection's difference type.
.Fn dtfl_diff_i64
is the default and the signed classes are Abelian (they support
negation);
.Fn dtfl_diff_u64
and the other unsigned classes are a commutative monoid; and
.Fn dtfl_diff_present
is a semigroup only, whose values never cancel.
.Fn dtfl_diff_retain
and
.Fn dtfl_diff_free
adjust the reference count.
.Fn dtfl_diff_width
is the byte width of a value, and
.Fn dtfl_diff_is_abelian
reports whether the class supports negation, which
.Fn dtfl_collection_negate
requires.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_type ,
.Fn dtfl_collection_diff
and
.Fn dtfl_collection_scope
report the record type, diff class and scope behind a collection.
.Fn dtfl_collection_free
releases the handle without touching the dataflow.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_map
and
.Fn dtfl_collection_flat_map
transform the record of each update, keeping its time and diff;
.Fn dtfl_collection_map
emits exactly one output record per input and
.Fn dtfl_collection_flat_map
emits zero or more.
Both callbacks write their output records with
.Fn dtfl_collection_emit_record ,
which supplies the record only; the operator attaches the time and
diff.
.Fn dtfl_collection_filter
keeps the updates whose record satisfies the predicate.
.Fn dtfl_collection_negate
flips the sign of every diff and requires an Abelian class.
.Fn dtfl_collection_concat
and
.Fn dtfl_collection_concatenate
accumulate the updates of several collections.
.Fn dtfl_collection_consolidate
groups updates by
.Pq record , time ,
sums their diffs, drops those that sum to zero and exchanges records
across workers, so the result holds at most one update per
.Pq record , time .
.Fn dtfl_collection_inspect
calls the callback for every update.
.Fn dtfl_collection_explode
replaces each record and multiplies its diff by a factor of
.Fa factor_diff ,
moving aggregatable data into the difference; its callback emits
.Pq record , factor
pairs with
.Fn dtfl_collection_emit_pair .
.Fn dtfl_collection_delay
re-times each update by a monotone function that only advances time.
.Fn dtfl_collection_enter
and
.Fn dtfl_collection_leave
move a collection across a scope boundary, projecting the embedded time
with the scope refinement.
.Fn dtfl_collection_enter_at
is like
.Fn dtfl_collection_enter ,
but each record appears in the child scope at a per-record initial inner
time that
.Fa logic
writes into its
.Fa inner_time_out
argument, which the operator pairs with the refined outer time.
.Fn dtfl_collection_probe
and
.Fn dtfl_collection_probe_with
attach a timely probe to the collection's output.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn dtfl_diff_*
constructors and the collection operators return a new handle owned by
the caller, except that a collection handle shares the worker's
dataflow.
.Fn dtfl_collection_explode
returns
.Dv NULL
when the multiply of the factor and input diff classes is undefined.
.Fn dtfl_diff_width
returns the value width and
.Fn dtfl_diff_is_abelian
returns a boolean.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static void dbl(void *ctx, const void *rec, size_t len,
    dtfl_collection_emit *out) {
	unsigned char buf[8];
	dtfl_put_u64(buf, dtfl_get_u64(rec) * 2);
	dtfl_collection_emit_record(out, buf, sizeof buf);
	(void)ctx; (void)len;
}

dtfl_diff *r = dtfl_diff_i64();
dtfl_input_session *in = dtfl_input_session_new(dtfl_type_u64(), r);
dtfl_collection *c = dtfl_input_session_to_collection(in, scope);
dtfl_collection *d = dtfl_collection_map(c, dtfl_type_u64(), dbl, DTFL_NOCTX);
dtfl_probe *p;
dtfl_collection *out = dtfl_collection_probe(
    dtfl_collection_consolidate(d), &p);
dtfl_collection_free(out);
dtfl_collection_free(d);
dtfl_collection_free(c);
dtfl_diff_free(r);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width DTFL_EALGEBRA
.It Bq Er DTFL_EALGEBRA
.Fn dtfl_collection_explode
has no multiply declared for the factor and input diff classes.
